	abstract = {The integration of Industry 4.0 technologies, particularly smart sensors and remote sensing, is transforming the seafood sector, enhancing productivity, sustainability, quality, and traceability in aquaculture, fisheries, post-harvest optimization, and seafood processing. This chapter explores the application of smart sensors in aquaculture, where real-time monitoring of water quality, environmental conditions, and fish health supports optimized feeding and waste reduction. In fisheries, remote sensing technologies like satellites and drones provide critical data for managing fish populations, tracking species, and monitoring ecological impacts. During post-harvest, smart sensors enable efficient quality control, ensuring the freshness and safety of seafood products along the supply chain. In processing and packaging, sensors maintain quality standards and enhance consumer trust through precise environmental monitoring and contamination prevention. By leveraging these technologies, the seafood sector can achieve greater operational efficiency and promote sustainable practices. This chapter examines the latest developments, practical applications, and future prospects for smart sensors and remote sensing in advancing aquaculture, fisheries, and the seafood industry. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved..},
