	affiliations = {INTI International University, Nilai, Negeri Sembilan, Malaysia; Schneider Electric Singapore, Singapore City, Singapore},
	abstract = {IoT and green manufacturing technologies offer transformative solutions for poultry farming, enhancing efficiency, productivity, and overall farm management. Through the integration of sensors and automation, these systems enable real-time monitoring of environmental conditions such as temperature, humidity, and air quality. Livestock tracking using RFID or GPS technology provides insights into individual bird health and behavior. Automated feeding systems and smart feeders optimize the feeding process, ensuring consistent and timely nourishment for the poultry. Water quality monitoring using IoT sensors guarantees access to clean water, a vital component for poultry health. Wearable health sensors and predictive analytics contribute to early disease detection and informed decision-making. Smart lighting systems, energy management, and supply chain optimization further improve operational processes. Remote monitoring and control through mobile apps or dashboards empower farmers to oversee the farm from anywhere, while integration with ERP systems streamlines overall management, including financial tracking and resource allocation. This holistic approach to IoT and green manufacturing in poultry farming ultimately results in improved efficiency, reduced costs, and enhanced productivity, all while prioritizing the well-being of the poultry. © 2024 IEEE.},
